# Base URL of the backend API.
#
# Leave EMPTY for local development — Vite proxies /api to http://localhost:4000,
# so same-origin requests work with no configuration.
#
# For production, set this ONLY if the frontend is served from a different origin
# than the API (e.g. the frontend is on a CDN). If you serve both behind the same
# domain and reverse-proxy /api to the backend (recommended, and required for
# SameSite=Lax session cookies to work), leave this empty there too.
#
# Example for a split-origin deployment:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.dashboard.example.com
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
